WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.601
-Our next guest is
a talented actress you know from

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.370
"Mission: Impossible -- Fallout"
and "Rogue Nation"

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.306
as well as films
like "Doctor Sleep"

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.473
and "The Greatest Showman."

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:09.609
She stars in "Dune,"
which is now in theaters

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.244
and IMAX and on HBO Max.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.278
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:15.214 line:0%
-You know the ancient tongues.

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:16.849
-I know many things.

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:21.521 line:0%
I know that you have a weapon
concealed in your bodice.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:25.024 line:0%
If you mean to harm me,
I must warn you,

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:30.763
whatever you're hiding,
it won't be enough.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:33.999
-The weapon is meant as a gift.

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:36.169
If you are truly the one.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:44.076 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:51.984 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:55.154
Do you know this?

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:56.823
-It's a crysknife.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:01:00.592 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:00.592 --> 00:01:02.262
-Do you know its meaning?

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.567
-Please welcome to the show
Rebecca Ferguson.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.335
How are you?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:12.271
-Hey, I'm good.

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:13.506
-We're so happy
to have you here.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.474
Congratulations on the film.

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:17.443
Also announced today,
there's going to be a sequel.

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:20.680
So that is great news as well.
-I just found out.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.215
-Yeah.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.851
-Are you putting that
on your media?

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.519
I mean, I am.
-Oh, absolutely.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.620
We're going to make
a big deal out of it.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.854
And with that sequel money,

00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:30.590
you can really splurge on
Halloween candy.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.825
[ Laughter ]
-I mean, that's what I'm doing.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.760
Big costume.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.495
-I know you have children.

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:39.498
Where do you get -- You're
a world traveler, as it were.

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:42.068
Where do you get to celebrate
Halloween this year?

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:46.072
-Well, we're thinking COVID
safety -- backyard.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.474
No, we're not. I mean, we are --

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:51.010
We're going to go knocking
door to door.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.981
I think it's more for me and
my husband more than my child.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.083
But we want to dress up
as something scary.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.551
She's thinking unicorn.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.086
So we'll see where we end up.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.354
-Oh, this is very interesting.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.721
The child doesn't want scary,

00:02:02.721 --> 00:02:06.291
but as parents you think
she should be more frightening?

00:02:06.291 --> 00:02:07.593
-Well, you know,
we need to kind of

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:09.795
get her slowly
into the scary world

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:11.831
because life isn't easy.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:12.999
Do you know what I mean?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:15.168
-Do you guys dress up as well?

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.870
-I mean, not on Halloween,
but other days.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.638
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:22.007
As evidenced by the clip
we just showed. I think.

00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:24.010
-Exactly. Well done.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.579
-I think that there is going to
be maybe a fair share

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.013
of "Dune" costumes this year.

00:02:28.013 --> 00:02:29.716
Have you considered that?

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:32.585
-I've already had people call me
and say they want to dress up.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:34.453
So I'm trying to gather
all my costume,

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:37.056
but now I'm going to have to
send it back due to the second.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.357
[ Laughter ]
-Right.

00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:40.526
You need it again.

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:43.462
-I shouldn't have stolen
those things.

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:46.966
-Your father is Swedish,
your mother is British.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.435
And this seems very on the nose.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.004
But when you were young,

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.339
your mother taught you
how to play bridge,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.575
which seems like just
the most stereotypical

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:58.177
British mother thing
I've ever heard.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:02.115
-I mean, she didn't teach me
how to play bridge.

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:05.684
She decided to sign me up
to a bridge...

00:03:05.684 --> 00:03:07.386
[ Laughs ]

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:11.558
To a bridge course with me
and three other ladies.

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:13.392
I was 15.

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:15.862
They were 85, 80.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.330
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.032
And that is not to be ageist.

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:23.269
I had fun, but I think
I was a counter.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.104
You know, I could count cards
very quickly,

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.772
so I got kicked out
of the group.

00:03:26.772 --> 00:03:28.274
[ Laughter ]
-Really?

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.142
I did not realize
it's against the rules

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:31.744
to count cards in bridge.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:34.680
-I just think you have to play
your cards right,

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.282
if you know what I mean.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.051
Ruth was not happy.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.318
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.821
-Of course, there is always
a Ruth who is not happy.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:44.724
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.759
-Are you a family
that plays games

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:47.794
together with your children?

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:50.029
-Yes. We do.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.531
My mom actually established
cards.

00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:55.001
So when I was young,
she would wake me up at --

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:56.769
I mean an hour before school.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.805
We lived [audio drop]
to the school where I went.

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:01.607
But she put on classical music
in the background.

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:04.043
And it sounds really romantic
and wonderful.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:06.345
She put Mozart on or something,

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.381
and then we'd play
three rounds of cards.

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:12.652
It would be canasta, two-man's
whist, and something else --

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:14.887
gin rummy or something.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:17.190
But then I had to guess
the music in the background.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.626
She'd go, "Darling, darling,
what are we listening to now?

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:21.126
Darling?"

00:04:21.126 --> 00:04:23.663
And then I had to literally go,
"Oh, God damn it.

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:26.032
Handel, Chopin, Mozart?
I don't know."

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:28.300
Just kind of wing it.
But it was --

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.137
I do the same without the music
now with my kids, yeah.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:33.239
-Your mom probably did it to you

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:35.407
to distract you
from counting the cards.

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:37.109
[ Laughter ]
-Well done.

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:39.946
That's exactly it.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:41.247
Well done.
I hadn't thought of that.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.315
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.315 --> 00:04:47.520
-Your son is a bit older,
maybe old enough to watch a film

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.155
like "Dune" or
the "Mission: Impossible" films.

00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:52.859
Does he watch your work and does
he think it's pretty cool

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.660
the kind of films his mom is in?

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.162
-Yeah, I mean, he does.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.997
He's also -- not to forget --
he was, I think, six years old

00:04:58.997 --> 00:05:00.499
when I did the first "Mission."

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:02.301
Five and a half, six.

00:05:02.301 --> 00:05:03.869
So he was a set baby.

00:05:03.869 --> 00:05:07.573
I mean, when I rocked up
into the stunt team,

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.208
he would be strapped up
in a harness.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.210
And they basically set them off
really high.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.446
And I'd be like, "Great, I'll be
back in three hours."

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:15.181
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.249
Joke, but not a joke, really.

00:05:17.249 --> 00:05:19.752
That was his world.

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:24.757
But then I think with "Dune,"
I think he was not prepared

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:27.760
for the emotional ride
that he went through.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.762
He was sitting next to me --
It was my second screening.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:32.064
I'd asked for another screening
because I really wanted to see

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:35.334
it with him before going on
the whole big world tour.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:38.270
And I thought he was going to be
most excited about

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:41.006
the big Jason Momoa sequences,

00:05:41.006 --> 00:05:44.543
and not to push Jason Momoa
down -- he's fantastic --

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:48.647
but my son was so excited about
the Hans Zimmer score

00:05:48.647 --> 00:05:51.650
that he'd, like, every second
grab my hand and go,

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.186
"So beautiful."

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.854
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:58.691
I was like, "Really?
Dude, come on. Shape up."

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.760
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.095
-It's very funny to think of
anybody having to choose

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:05.464
between Jason Momoa
and Hans Zimmer.

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:08.567
I feel like that's not a choice
people are making that often.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.069
-Not "rock/hard place," is it?

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.270
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.173
Jason Momoa and Dave Bautista
were on our show

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:16.375
talking about -- obviously,
you did a great many

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:19.478
location shoots
for a film of this scope.

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:23.549
Was there a place that you
particularly were drawn to?

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:26.652
-What was Momoa drawn to?
Did he tell you?

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:29.188
-It was very hard to understand
either of them.

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:30.522
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, right.

00:06:30.522 --> 00:06:32.458
I was just going to say wherever
Jason Momoa goes, I go.

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:33.459
You know?
-Yeah, exactly.

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:36.095
-So his location.

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:41.100
No, I -- Abu Dhabi,
Wadi Rum was amazing.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.736
I mean, the desert. There is
something -- Have you been?

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.571
Have you been to the desert?
-I've never been, no.

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.339
-You haven't?

00:06:47.339 --> 00:06:49.741
-No. Well, had you been
before you were in "Dune"?

00:06:49.741 --> 00:06:53.445
[ Laughter ]
-No. I know.

00:06:53.445 --> 00:06:56.249
I literally just thought,
"What a weird comment."

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:57.817
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.817 --> 00:07:00.620
No. No, Seth. That is true.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:04.757
However, there is something
about being so small

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:09.161
in that enormous landscape
that is very, very humbling.

00:07:09.161 --> 00:07:12.397
And people like us
need that sometimes.

00:07:12.397 --> 00:07:14.400
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.536
-So I would see Jason Momoa
on a hill,

00:07:17.536 --> 00:07:20.339
and Timothee would be
on the other hill,

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:22.875
and we'd just sit there.

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:25.244
-Often when my wife and I
are arguing, she will say,

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:28.313
"You need to go to Abu Dhabi..."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.313 --> 00:07:31.817
"...and get your ego in check."

00:07:31.817 --> 00:07:33.452
-She will now.

00:07:33.452 --> 00:07:37.823
-Yeah. "You need to go sit
on a hill in Abu Dhabi."

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:40.926
-Or actually, you know what,
Seth, can I tell you?

00:07:40.926 --> 00:07:44.563
-Yeah.
-I'm going off piece.

00:07:44.563 --> 00:07:47.699
-Great.
-I was in Wadi Rum.

00:07:47.699 --> 00:07:51.537
And I was going in one of
those 4x4s, going up and down

00:07:51.537 --> 00:07:54.973
the sand dunes on my day off.

00:07:54.973 --> 00:07:57.409
Obviously, I didn't do that.
I haven't done any of that.

00:07:57.409 --> 00:08:00.079
I didn't sign any papers.

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:02.448
But all of a sudden the guy
basically goes,

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:03.749
"Oh, my God, look at the stone."

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:06.118
And I thought,
"Sure, that's a big stone."

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:08.220
And he goes,
"That's where Matt Damon sat

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:12.158
when he did 'The Martian.'"
And I thought, "No!

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:14.126
I don't want to know that."

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:15.427
[ Laughter ]

00:08:15.427 --> 00:08:19.731
"That just kills it for me.
That's a tiny rock, man."

00:08:19.731 --> 00:08:21.167
-Yeah, you're like,

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:23.469
"This is the most amazing piece
of nature I've ever seen."

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:25.204
They're like,
"Nope, you're on a movie set."

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:27.239
[ Laughter ]
-"No. You're on a movie set."

00:08:27.239 --> 00:08:29.675
Been here.

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:32.011
-Even people who have seen
the trailer would know

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:34.814
how terrifying the sandworms
in this film are.

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:37.116
But I hear sweethearts
to work with.

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:38.484
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:40.485
-Oh, my gosh, they're beautiful.

00:08:40.485 --> 00:08:41.954
I have them in my contract now.

00:08:41.954 --> 00:08:45.291
Just humbling, you know,
harming, small.

00:08:45.291 --> 00:08:46.525
[ Laughter ]

00:08:46.525 --> 00:08:49.895
They are -- The worst thing is
I wish I had --

00:08:49.895 --> 00:08:51.764
We had sex names for everything.

00:08:51.764 --> 00:08:53.432
Obviously I can't tell you.

00:08:53.432 --> 00:08:56.535
But the ornithopters
were horny throppers.

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:58.671
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.671 --> 00:09:00.372
I can't remember
the sandworm names.

00:09:00.372 --> 00:09:01.506
I think we should move on.

00:09:01.506 --> 00:09:03.409
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:03.409 --> 00:09:05.477
I think collectively
everybody agrees

00:09:05.477 --> 00:09:06.679
that's the right thing to do.

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:07.913
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:09.915
-Or not. Or not.

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:11.717
-Next time you have to share
all of them.

00:09:11.717 --> 00:09:13.118
Hey, thank you so much.

00:09:13.118 --> 00:09:15.721
Congrats again on
the news of the sequel,

00:09:15.721 --> 00:09:17.856
and we look forward
to seeing you next time.

00:09:17.856 --> 00:09:19.592
-I'll see you.
Thank you for having me.

00:09:19.592 --> 00:09:20.926
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:20.926 --> 00:09:23.529
-"Dune" is in theaters and IMAX
and on HBO Max now.

